narrator: Marisol arrives on time. To the minute.
narrator: She isn't carrying the notebook.
narrator: She also isn't carrying the cigarette holder.
join marisol (Neutral) leftmost
player: "No holder today."
marisol: "I put it away. It was becoming a prop."
narrator: She sits. Without theatrics.
narrator: Something has shifted. You're not entirely sure if that's better or worse.
marisol: "I finished the chapter."
player: "Which chapter?"
marisol: "The one about the therapist."
narrator: A pause.
marisol: "And then I deleted it."
player: "How did that feel?"
marisol: "Like putting a book back on the shelf. It was adequate. As a chapter. But it wasn't what I was trying to write."
[stat_check stat="patience"]
if {check_result}:
	do GameState.add_stat_xp("patience", 1)
	narrator: You wait. She's working up to something. Interrupting now would be like breaking tension in chapter twenty-three.
	marisol: "I wrote the ending."
	player: "Of the therapist chapter?"
	marisol: "Of Rodrigo's book."
	narrator: A beat.
	marisol: "He goes home."
	player: "That's the ending?"
	marisol: "He stops sailing. He sells the ship. He buys a house with a very boring garden and he learns the names of his neighbors."
	narrator: A beat.
	player: "That's not a typical ending for the series."
	marisol: "No. It isn't."
	do PatientManager.add_trust("marisol", 8)
else:
	player: "You deleted it."
	marisol: "I deleted it."
	narrator: A beat.
	marisol: "I may have also written the ending of Rodrigo's book."
	do PatientManager.add_trust("marisol", 3)
[photo_opportunity id="marisol_dedication" patient="marisol" title="The Dedication Page" description="The handwritten dedication of The Corsair's Surrender. Visible just long enough to read one line." portrait="res://assets/photos/marisol/dedication.png"]
if {flags.last_photo_success}:
	narrator: She's watching your face. This time she doesn't look like she's mapping responses. She just looks like she wants to know what you think.
	do PatientManager.add_trust("marisol", 3)
- What did you learn from writing him? | [if {patients.marisol.trust} >= 50] [else="disable" alt_text="need 50 trust"]
	marisol: "That I am a very good novelist."
	narrator: A beat.
	marisol: "And that I have been using very good novelists as an excuse not to be a person."
	narrator: She says it lightly. It lands hard.
	do PatientManager.add_trust("marisol", 12)
- What happens in Rodrigo's ending?
	marisol: "He stops performing the adventure. He starts living the ordinary one."
	narrator: She says it as though reciting someone else's work.
	do PatientManager.add_trust("marisol", 5)
if {patients.marisol.trust} >= 70 and {flags.marisol_named_escapism_s2}:
	marisol: "I've been thinking about what you said. About the block not being in the writing."
	player: "And?"
	marisol: "And I think you were — broadly, in the approximate vicinity of — not wrong."
	narrator: She smooths her skirt.
	marisol: "There's a support group. For people in creative fields. They meet on Thursdays."
	player: "That's a real thing you're considering."
	marisol: "It's research."
	narrator: She says it differently than she used to.
	player: "Of course."
	marisol: "The book will be done next month. I want to dedicate it properly."
	narrator: She pauses at the door.
	marisol: "Thank you, Doctor. For reading carefully."
	set {patients.marisol.ending} = "breakthrough"
	[add_note patient="marisol" note="Breakthrough. Finished Rodrigo's arc, deleted the therapist chapter, considering the Thursday group. The dedication is presumably significant."]
else:
	if {patients.marisol.trust} < 30:
		narrator: She stands. Gathers her things with ceremony.
		marisol: "I appreciate your time, Doctor. Deeply."
		narrator: She produces a card.
		marisol: "My publisher is always looking for authentic settings. This office would be useful. For research."
		narrator: A pause.
		marisol: "I'll be in touch."
		narrator: She leaves. You notice the card has her home address written on the back.
		leave marisol
		set {patients.marisol.ending} = "bad"
		[add_note patient="marisol" note="Declined therapeutic framework. Now treating the practice as a research location. Left her home address. Unknown whether this is a concern or a publishing strategy."]
	else:
		marisol: "Anyway. Rodrigo will get there eventually."
		player: "I think he will."
		marisol: "He's very stubborn. But thorough. He'll arrive at the right place in the right chapter."
		narrator: She stands. Her hand moves toward where the cigarette holder usually is. Stops. Falls to her side.
		marisol: "Progress."
		narrator: She says it like a plot point.
		set {patients.marisol.ending} = "stuck"
		[add_note patient="marisol" note="Inconclusive arc. Still narrating rather than experiencing. But Rodrigo is going home eventually. That might be something."]
leave marisol
do PatientManager.mark_session_done("marisol")
jump between_patients/